1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,740
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,240
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:05,910
(Episode 19)

4
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,180
What is tteok-twi-sun?

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,720
I've never heard of it.

6
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,450
Tteokbokki, fritters, and sundae
eaten together...

7
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:17,920
are called "tteok-twi-sun" for short.

8
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:20,590
You must not eat street food
very often.

9
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:25,200
I thought she was going to buy me
something amazing.

10
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,000
Why would I not know
what tteokbokki, fritters, and sundae...

11
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:31,700
Where did she go?
Ms. Kang Da Mi. Kang...

12
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:33,910
(Cotton Candy)

13
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:45,380
Buy it for me.
I really want to eat it.

14
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:49,020
Mom. Just this one time.

15
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:51,420
Please.

16
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:56,030
Will you stop it?
Why are you acting like this?

17
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,660
I told you I didn't have any money!

18
00:00:58,130 --> 00:01:00,700
Why are you hitting me?
You're so mean, Mom.

19
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,830
(Cotton Candy, 3 dollars)

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,300
If you want to eat it, just buy it.

21
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,940
Why are you just standing there
staring at it?

22
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:11,210
No, it's not that I want to eat it.

23
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:14,950
It just reminded me of something.

24
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,720
You go through life thinking
you are a good liar, don't you?

25
00:01:21,590 --> 00:01:23,720
Who said I was lying?
It's the truth.

26
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:24,860
Whatever.

27
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:27,690
Since you said you are buying
the tteok-twi-sun,

28
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:30,130
I'll buy the cotton candy
as an appetizer.

29
00:01:31,130 --> 00:01:33,360
Sir, I would like
one cotton candy, please.

30
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:43,140
Hey, you can't pay with a card.
I'm sorry, sir.

31
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,340
Where is my wallet?

32
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,980
It's three dollars, right?
Here you go, sir.

33
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,450
I told you I was buying it.

34
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:54,620
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

35
00:01:54,750 --> 00:01:56,320
- Goodbye.
- Have a good day.

36
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,330
Why can't I pay with my card?

37
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:05,000
People who run stalls like that
usually don't accept cards.

38
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,600
They don't make that much money.

39
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,870
And they often can't come out to sell
when it rains.

40
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:11,740
They live day to day.

41
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:17,140
You are always nagging me
to observe people more closely.

42
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:22,750
Is the cotton candy good?

43
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:26,380
No, it's just okay.

44
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,450
This only tastes good
when someone else buys it.

45
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,190
Look at you, lying again.

46
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:33,490
Give me one bite.
I need to try it to find out the truth.

47
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:37,130
Just one bite...

48
00:02:38,130 --> 00:02:39,360
Give me a bite. Hey.

49
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,900
Are the shoes comfortable?

50
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:44,870
They're fine.

51
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:47,110
But don't you think
there is an issue...

52
00:02:47,110 --> 00:02:48,610
with that employee,
Manager Kang, ma'am?

53
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:52,240
How can the personal shopper
in charge...

54
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,780
take a day off on the day
you are visiting?

55
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:57,950
Should I file a complaint
with the department store?

56
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:01,150
Leave it.
It's only strike two for now.

57
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:02,390
Come on, Mom.

58
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:06,120
- That rainbow cotton candy, please?
- No.

59
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:09,960
I don't care. I want to eat it.

60
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:12,730
- You are a good son, right?
- Yes.

61
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:18,970
You're so mean, Mom.

62
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:20,170
(Cotton Candy, 3 dollars)

63
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,610
Just wait until we get home.

64
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:25,580
You're in big trouble.

65
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,980
Child, I'll give you one.
Here you go.

66
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:29,680
Stop crying.
You're a good girl, right?

67
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:31,980
Take it back, ma'am.

68
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,290
Listen, ma'am.

69
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:37,190
It looks like you are
having a hard time,

70
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:39,720
but that does not mean you should
take your anger out on the child.

71
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:42,630
Just go. I won't take your money.

72
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:45,830
Who are you to lecture me?

73
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:47,200
Do you know me?

74
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:58,140
(Cotton Candy, 3 dollars)

75
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,720
- Ma'am?
- This is crazy.

76
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:06,020
- Here you go.
- Hold on.

77
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:08,020
Why are you being like this?

78
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,690
- Get up.
- No.

79
00:04:10,990 --> 00:04:12,520
(Sweet Cotton Candy!)

80
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,930
- I want to eat it.
- Get up. No.

81
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:16,630
Here.

82
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:19,530
Thank you.

83
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:22,800
Excuse me, who are you...

84
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:24,440
to give him that
without my permission?

85
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:26,200
Wait, are you...

86
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:29,340
the CEO of Hwanggeum Apparel?

87
00:04:31,010 --> 00:04:33,950
I saw you on television
doing an interview recently.

88
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:37,120
- I saw that interview too.
- She looks like a model in person.

89
00:04:37,220 --> 00:04:38,750
- It's really her.
- She is so pretty.

90
00:04:38,850 --> 00:04:41,150
Kids remember moments like this...

91
00:04:41,150 --> 00:04:43,290
as happy memories
long after they've grown up.

92
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:46,690
I wanted to give him
a good memory like that.

93
00:04:46,690 --> 00:04:47,730
Is that okay?

94
00:04:47,990 --> 00:04:49,130
Yes, of course.

95
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,060
Could you take a picture with us?

96
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,400
Of course.

97
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:58,940
Look here.

98
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,240
- Could you take a picture with us?
- I should casually post online...

99
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,150
that I witnessed
a heartwarming moment.

100
00:05:07,150 --> 00:05:08,380
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

101
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:10,150
One, two.

102
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,750
I followed you on social media too.

103
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,490
- You are the best.
- Thank you.

104
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:15,850
We need to go now, ma'am.

105
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:17,460
They contacted us
to say they arrived first.

106
00:05:17,590 --> 00:05:18,820
All right. Let's go.

107
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:22,330
Thank you.

108
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,600
Why is he alone?

109
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:36,710
The two junior employees
are at the hotel...

110
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:38,940
doing a final check
on the contract details.

111
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:42,610
They said they will arrive soon
if you two start talking first.

112
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,680
Okay.

113
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,690
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting.

114
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:57,400
It's really nice to meet you.

115
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:00,470
It's great to see you too.
I just got here anyway.

116
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:01,630
Please have a seat.

117
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,140
Are you okay, ma'am?

118
00:06:09,170 --> 00:06:11,740
Goodness.
Let me get someone to help.

119
00:06:12,010 --> 00:06:13,010
Stop.

120
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,450
But...

121
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,810
I said be quiet.

122
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,180
Can't you see everyone is watching?

123
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:19,880
Yes, ma'am.

124
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,790
My ankle hurts too much.

125
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,170
Seems like your shoes are suggesting
that we postpone today's meeting.

126
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:43,210
My apologies. Please excuse us.

127
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:46,380
I'll check on our CEO's condition
and get back to you.

128
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:49,450
Ma'am, he said we should postpone...

129
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:50,520
Enough.

130
00:06:51,550 --> 00:06:53,080
I can understand that much.

131
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:04,960
My apologies,
but I have to leave now.

132
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:08,070
- I'll contact you shortly.
- I hope you are okay.

133
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:13,070
Please, just go.

134
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,040
Excuse me.

135
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:48,810
Aren't you in a meeting? What's up?

136
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:50,780
Our target has managed to fall...

137
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:53,280
and take herself out
before the meeting even started.

138
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:56,480
No, really. She actually fell,

139
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:00,220
and her staff had to help her out
literally right after she got here.

140
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:02,450
Okay. Got it.

141
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:04,190
I bet she didn't like that.

142
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:07,060
She's not the type to get away
with mistakes.

143
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:08,460
She's never made any.

144
00:08:08,830 --> 00:08:10,090
You had to see that.

145
00:08:11,530 --> 00:08:13,300
Where are you at, buddy? You out?

146
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:17,800
Yes. Just checking out the area.
I should head in.

147
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:20,340
My group is waiting for me.
Bye, Danny.

148
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:28,380
My body aches all over.

149
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,620
I barely moved much today...

150
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:33,680
and I'm aching all over.

151
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:39,920
If Mi Mi's family catches me,
they will pull all my hair out.

152
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,060
What should I do?

153
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:45,760
Who cares, right?
I need money right now.

154
00:08:50,230 --> 00:08:51,240
Goodness.

155
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:53,910
Where exactly did you get a job?

156
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:58,210
Well, you'll find out
eventually anyway.

157
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,810
There's a clinic called
Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine.

158
00:09:02,410 --> 00:09:04,980
I got a job there
as a desk receptionist.

159
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:32,410
You got here faster than I thought.

160
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,080
What about Summit Investment?

161
00:09:34,210 --> 00:09:36,680
He decided to reschedule
for another day and left.

162
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,350
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

163
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:41,920
Mom.

164
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,390
Why didn't you take her
straight to the hospital?

165
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:48,930
I was going to, but she said
she wanted to go home.

166
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:53,130
What good would it be to have
an article written about this?

167
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:56,100
I don't want to give people
a reason to gossip.

168
00:09:57,370 --> 00:09:58,370
This way.

169
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,380
Ma'am, please lean back comfortably.

170
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:24,560
The meeting was suddenly canceled,
and I heard you got hurt.

171
00:10:25,130 --> 00:10:27,030
I was so shocked
when Assistant Manager Kang called me.

172
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,250
(Hwanggeum Capital)

173
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:43,950
(CEO Cha In Sung)

174
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:51,420
What happened?

175
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:54,790
Why would she fall when she was
on her way to a meeting?

176
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:58,230
Where and how badly
did she get hurt?

177
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:02,170
Yes, sir.

178
00:11:02,530 --> 00:11:05,470
Cancel all my evening appointments.
I'm heading home right now.

179
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,970
Get the car ready, quickly.

180
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:31,030
Wait, when did you even get
in the car, Assistant Manager Kang?

181
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:33,700
CEO Jeon was in so much pain.

182
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:35,530
It's only right
that I escort her home.

183
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:38,570
Why are you fulfilling a duty
that no one even asked you to do?

184
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:42,010
Please take a taxi and go.
You can claim the fare back later.

185
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:43,870
It will be hard for you
to manage alone, Team Leader Cha.

186
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,710
Since I'm already here,
I'll help you take her inside...

187
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:49,050
That is enough. You can go.
Thank you for your help.

188
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:51,620
Yes, sir.

189
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:53,980
Let's go.

190
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:58,860
I've never been so humiliated
in my life.

191
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:06,730
Please take care, ma'am.
I'll see you at the office.

192
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:09,170
What happened today
is off the record.

193
00:12:09,670 --> 00:12:10,670
Yes, Team Leader Cha.

194
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,840
This is even more incredible
than I imagined.

195
00:12:21,010 --> 00:12:23,050
Look at those
polished garden decorations...

196
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:24,150
and the trees.

197
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:26,250
This place is seriously no joke.

198
00:12:28,250 --> 00:12:29,250
That's right, Kang Ye Ri.

199
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:33,160
Just you wait. I'm definitely going
to marry into this family.

200
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:37,860
What is going on?

201
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:40,300
Why is Do Yun's mother
coming home at this hour?

202
00:12:40,970 --> 00:12:44,370
It seems like she got hurt
somewhere, Madam.

203
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,470
Where?

204
00:12:46,270 --> 00:12:48,410
If she's hurt,
she should go to the hospital.

205
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:51,440
Goodness...

206
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:54,080
Where could she have gotten hurt?

207
00:12:55,450 --> 00:12:56,580
Where?

208
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:07,420
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

209
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:09,160
No way.

210
00:13:09,630 --> 00:13:11,500
I thought it was strange
when I looked at the map.

211
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:13,400
This is...

212
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,010
Why would she leave
her desk empty...

213
00:13:22,070 --> 00:13:24,140
on her very first day of work
and go somewhere else?

214
00:13:27,810 --> 00:13:29,980
Well, the clinic is quite clean.

215
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:37,560
Hello.
I came to this clinic today...

216
00:13:37,690 --> 00:13:41,130
to see my wife, who is
a certified nursing assistant,

217
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:42,860
start her first day
as a desk receptionist.

218
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:46,360
Since it has been so long
since she last worked,

219
00:13:46,430 --> 00:13:48,100
I wanted to come and support her.

220
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Wait, how are you here...

221
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:58,210
Thank you again for today, sir.
Take care.

222
00:13:58,610 --> 00:13:59,780
Have a good day.

223
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:02,450
Yes, thank you, sir.

224
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:03,880
Always drive safely.

225
00:14:05,350 --> 00:14:06,720
Weren't you the taxi driver?

226
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:10,250
So my passenger was a doctor.

227
00:14:11,590 --> 00:14:14,590
What are the odds
of meeting again like this?

228
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:18,500
I know, right?
It's so nice to see you like this.

229
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:21,630
- Yes.
- So, you're saying your wife...

230
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:23,270
is Park Ji Young,

231
00:14:23,270 --> 00:14:25,640
who started her first day
working at our clinic today?

232
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,770
Yes, that's right. She is my wife.

233
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:31,340
But where is she right now?

234
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:33,980
Since she came into work
so suddenly today,

235
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,480
I told her to get off work early.

236
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:37,080
It also seemed like
she had an upset stomach.

237
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:38,980
An upset stomach?

238
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:42,620
She has never had
stomach issues in her entire life.

239
00:14:44,490 --> 00:14:45,520
Is that so?

240
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:46,860
Yes.

241
00:14:48,690 --> 00:14:49,730
Goodness.

242
00:14:52,030 --> 00:14:53,300
Why is my stomach suddenly...

243
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,830
You must be very hungry.

244
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,300
Do you happen to like chicken soup?

245
00:14:59,370 --> 00:15:01,540
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup is
across from us.

246
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:02,540
Let's go together.

247
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:04,210
I was actually just starting
to feel hungry myself.

248
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:05,880
Goodness, wait.

249
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:10,050
No, that's quite alright.
You must be busy.

250
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,820
You don't have to do that.

251
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:16,790
No, I just got some free time,
so it's fine.

252
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:18,190
Wait, hold on a second.

253
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,930
I'm suddenly getting a lot of calls.

254
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:25,460
I'll greet you again next time then.

255
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,730
It was nice meeting you, Doctor.

256
00:15:27,730 --> 00:15:28,930
Then wait just a moment, sir.

257
00:15:30,070 --> 00:15:31,270
At least take this...

258
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:36,870
He must be very busy.

259
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,980
Goodness.

260
00:15:41,350 --> 00:15:42,380
My gosh.

261
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:45,720
My knee.

262
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,050
Darn it.

263
00:15:51,690 --> 00:15:53,490
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

264
00:15:57,190 --> 00:15:59,700
Wait, who is that?

265
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,540
I can't be dreaming.

266
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:09,240
That flat back of the head...

267
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:12,010
and that unusual zigzag walk...

268
00:16:12,710 --> 00:16:16,280
definitely belong to my own son,
Hak Sung.

269
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:19,920
Hey! Kang Hak Sung!

270
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,920
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

271
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:30,190
Is it not him?

272
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,730
Did I see that wrong?

273
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,670
No,

274
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:40,400
I'm absolutely sure.

275
00:16:42,110 --> 00:16:43,410
No.

276
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:46,640
He's supposedly doing well
with business in the Philippines,

277
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:49,210
so why would he be
wandering around here?

278
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:52,450
My days are numbered,

279
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,920
so my eyes must be
playing tricks on me.

280
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:56,090
Right, if I had
actually seen that jerk,

281
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:58,660
I would have killed him on the spot.

282
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:04,830
- Mother.
- You startled me.

283
00:17:05,930 --> 00:17:07,230
Why are you standing out here?

284
00:17:07,970 --> 00:17:09,130
You went out
to take out the trash...

285
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:11,100
and didn't come back for a while,
so I came out to check.

286
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,600
Why?

287
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,440
Did you follow me out here...

288
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,340
because you thought
I wouldn't be able to find my way back?

289
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:19,610
Why are you keeping an eye on me
and making me feel bad?

290
00:17:21,150 --> 00:17:23,150
I'm not keeping an eye
on you, Mother.

291
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:28,050
I just came out
because I was worried.

292
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:45,170
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

293
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:51,880
Do you think she heard me
calling out for Hak Sung...

294
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:56,110
No. She probably didn't hear it.

295
00:17:57,850 --> 00:17:59,850
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

296
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:07,220
What are you doing, Ri Ja?

297
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:09,590
Are you not preparing
for the dinner rush?

298
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,900
Customers will be flooding in
any minute now.

299
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:17,100
Oh, Mrs. Choi.
I finished that a long time ago.

300
00:18:17,630 --> 00:18:18,700
This is really delicious.

301
00:18:19,370 --> 00:18:21,270
Would you like some more, Mrs. Choi?

302
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:25,040
Your nerve pain is acting up again,
right, Mother?

303
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:28,610
We can handle the dinner rush
by ourselves,

304
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:30,850
so please go inside
and lie down, okay?

305
00:18:31,380 --> 00:18:33,720
Please do.
Don't worry about the restaurant.

306
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:35,890
I'm fine.

307
00:18:36,850 --> 00:18:39,020
It feels like a rain shower
is about to pass through...

308
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:40,960
because my joints are throbbing.

309
00:18:41,930 --> 00:18:44,730
It'll subside again soon.

310
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:47,760
It'll probably just be
a quick shower, Mrs. Choi.

311
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:50,870
You know, Mrs. Choi,

312
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:53,470
you are much more accurate
than a weather forecaster.

313
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:56,170
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

314
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,440
- Where are you going?
- What?

315
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:02,380
Me?

316
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,250
To Dr. Ju's clinic.

317
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:06,420
Why are you going there?

318
00:19:07,550 --> 00:19:09,950
I was wondering if he had
any rice cakes left.

319
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:13,090
How many mouths
do we have to feed at home?

320
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,590
Are just the three of us
going to eat them?

321
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:17,460
You and I are daughters
of a rice cake shop owner.

322
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:18,700
It has been a while, right?

323
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:21,330
Rice cakes that are this mild
and keep you coming back for more.

324
00:19:22,630 --> 00:19:25,900
How did Dr. Ju
choose such a good rice cake shop?

325
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:28,810
You've lost your mind again.

326
00:19:29,510 --> 00:19:31,070
Who are you trying
to embarrass this time?

327
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:33,540
Stop making a fuss
and just prepare for the dinner rush.

328
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:35,980
Hurry up and listen to me.

329
00:19:39,350 --> 00:19:41,920
That was definitely
the back of my son's head.

330
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:43,850
What in the world is going on?

331
00:19:46,090 --> 00:19:48,730
Mother, I'm going to step
into the main house for a bit.

332
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:51,190
I need to bring in the laundry...

333
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,730
and cover the jars in the yard
before the rain.

334
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,270
Mother.

335
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:01,970
Why do you keep calling me?
Are you a child?

336
00:20:02,210 --> 00:20:04,710
You can just take care
of it yourself.

337
00:20:08,210 --> 00:20:09,980
Why does she keep acting like that?

338
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:12,180
Did you make a mistake or something?

339
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:16,390
I committed the high treason
of raising my sons poorly.

340
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:21,060
Is she feeling more on edge
because of her leg?

341
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:29,270
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

342
00:20:35,970 --> 00:20:37,010
Mom, take it slow.

343
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:38,610
Hold on a second.

344
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,110
Oh, no.

345
00:20:41,850 --> 00:20:43,210
- Oh, no.
- Over there.

346
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:45,820
Gently.

347
00:20:48,890 --> 00:20:49,890
What should we do?

348
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:55,730
I've contacted Director Park.
He will be here within an hour, Mom.

349
00:20:55,830 --> 00:20:57,130
Okay, thank you for your help, Son.

350
00:20:57,890 --> 00:21:00,300
Don't worry about your mom,
and hurry back to the office.

351
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:03,330
I heard you were planning
a new proposal...

352
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:06,740
for sneakers that match skirts.
Assistant Manager Kang told me.

353
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,770
I still have plenty of time.

354
00:21:09,170 --> 00:21:10,940
I'll wait until
Director Park arrives.

355
00:21:11,210 --> 00:21:13,210
It's strictly working hours,

356
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:15,480
yet you left for personal matters,

357
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,780
and now you have the nerve
to say that?

358
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:18,820
Do you think
the team leader position...

359
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:20,280
is just something you do for fun?

360
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:22,690
Do Yun, you need to leave right now.

361
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:26,560
It looks like
you sprained your ankle,

362
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:28,730
so there is no need
for Director Park to come.

363
00:21:29,930 --> 00:21:31,060
I've separately...

364
00:21:31,130 --> 00:21:34,060
called someone who is good
at setting bones,

365
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,000
so just bear with it
for a little bit.

366
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:43,540
What are you standing around for?
Are you deaf?

367
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:47,240
No. I'll leave.
I'm leaving, Grandma.

368
00:21:52,450 --> 00:21:54,580
Who did Mother say she called?

369
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:56,250
Dr. Ju.

370
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:58,190
What?

371
00:22:25,350 --> 00:22:28,050
(Da Mi's Wedding Fund)

372
00:22:32,990 --> 00:22:35,060
(Regular Payment 200 Dollars,
Total 80,000 Dollars)

373
00:22:37,530 --> 00:22:39,100
They say children
are lifelong creditors...

374
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:40,400
born to collect debts,

375
00:22:41,130 --> 00:22:43,200
and Mother was absolutely right.

376
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:49,270
This is the money I saved up
to give Da Mi when she gets married.

377
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:52,010
When I think about my Da Mi,

378
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,610
I should never touch this.

379
00:22:57,610 --> 00:22:58,850
But what else can I do?

380
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,590
I have to save the one
who is in deep trouble first.

381
00:23:04,350 --> 00:23:05,820
I'll just make Dae Chi...

382
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:08,960
pay for our precious youngest's
wedding expenses...

383
00:23:09,690 --> 00:23:11,190
later on.

384
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:20,740
(Kang Da Mi, My Youngest)

385
00:23:26,510 --> 00:23:27,910
She said she took the day off today,

386
00:23:29,010 --> 00:23:30,650
so where is she?

387
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,450
I was going to tell her
while I had the courage.

388
00:23:40,060 --> 00:23:42,460
Grandma, I'm back from kindergarten.

389
00:23:43,690 --> 00:23:45,530
Welcome home, my granddaughter.

390
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:47,900
You did great today.

391
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:52,640
What are you going to do?

392
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:56,070
If you're even a day late
for your living expenses,

393
00:23:56,410 --> 00:23:58,680
your grandmother said
to send you packing.

394
00:23:59,010 --> 00:24:00,710
Of course.

395
00:24:00,780 --> 00:24:05,120
Grandma would definitely
kick me out ruthlessly.

396
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:08,050
Stop glaring at me like that, Mom.

397
00:24:09,050 --> 00:24:10,690
I'm looking for work.

398
00:24:13,060 --> 00:24:15,030
Did Dae Chi say
he would be late from work today?

399
00:24:16,190 --> 00:24:18,860
When does he ever
get off work early?

400
00:24:19,460 --> 00:24:21,800
Knowing him,
he'll work overtime every day...

401
00:24:22,370 --> 00:24:24,500
to earn a big bonus
and pay off his debt.

402
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:26,940
Pathetic jerk.

403
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:30,070
No matter how lacking I am,
I'm still his older brother.

404
00:24:30,410 --> 00:24:31,980
Before things got that out of hand,

405
00:24:32,210 --> 00:24:34,710
he should have at least
discussed it with me.

406
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:36,950
That's his problem.

407
00:24:37,350 --> 00:24:38,780
Ever since he was this little,

408
00:24:38,950 --> 00:24:41,750
he has thought he was
the smartest person in the world.

409
00:24:42,420 --> 00:24:43,520
I don't want to hear it.

410
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:46,890
Both you and Dae Chi
are my own flesh and blood.

411
00:24:47,890 --> 00:24:49,760
Why didn't you think
to check on him first?

412
00:24:49,830 --> 00:24:50,990
Do you not feel bad for him?

413
00:24:51,330 --> 00:24:53,030
Are you not sorry
as his older brother?

414
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:55,570
There you go again, Mom.

415
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:58,540
Why are you blaming me?

416
00:24:58,940 --> 00:25:00,570
Did I get into
1,130,000 dollars of debt?

417
00:25:01,370 --> 00:25:02,940
You always coddle him.

418
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:04,940
Your perfect second son.

419
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:06,940
You're always protecting
and covering for him.

420
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:09,650
When Dae Chi asks for anything,

421
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:11,780
you don't even ask questions.
You just do everything for him.

422
00:25:12,420 --> 00:25:13,680
Look at you right now.

423
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:15,850
Honestly, Mom,

424
00:25:16,450 --> 00:25:18,050
you want to do whatever it takes...

425
00:25:18,420 --> 00:25:20,360
to pay off all of Dae Chi's debt,
right?

426
00:25:21,890 --> 00:25:23,260
You can't fool me.

427
00:25:24,490 --> 00:25:27,900
No. To a mother,
every child is equally precious.

428
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:32,370
Why are you the one
breaking my heart like this?

429
00:25:32,700 --> 00:25:34,970
Of course every child is precious.

430
00:25:36,370 --> 00:25:39,610
But some are more precious
than others,

431
00:25:40,610 --> 00:25:43,210
and some are definitely less.

432
00:25:44,050 --> 00:25:45,950
Because you've been exactly
like that since we were young.

433
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,450
Just take Su Ah inside and wash her.

434
00:25:50,190 --> 00:25:51,660
Why am I even talking to you?

435
00:25:53,160 --> 00:25:55,590
Su Ah, let's go inside.
Dad will make you omurice.

436
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:57,530
Really? You mean it?

437
00:25:58,160 --> 00:25:59,160
Hey, sweetie,

438
00:25:59,660 --> 00:26:02,370
I asked you to at least
trust your dad.

439
00:26:02,430 --> 00:26:03,430
Did you forget?

440
00:26:08,170 --> 00:26:09,410
I met with Mi Seon for a bit.

441
00:26:11,710 --> 00:26:14,080
What did she say? Is she doing okay?

442
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:15,480
Doing okay? Please.

443
00:26:16,010 --> 00:26:17,150
Get this. She told me...

444
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:20,750
It's so ridiculous.

445
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:24,850
She told me to make chicken soup
in your restaurant's kitchen.

446
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:27,360
Summer is already over.
Has she lost her mind from the heat?

447
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,490
Is she trying to ruin the business?

448
00:26:29,490 --> 00:26:30,860
What?

449
00:26:30,860 --> 00:26:33,700
I have zero intention
of doing that either. Okay?

450
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:37,500
Chicken soup...
Let's go and eat some omurice.

451
00:26:47,710 --> 00:26:50,680
(Regular Payment 200 Dollars,
Total 80,000 Dollars)

452
00:26:53,420 --> 00:26:54,520
I'm sorry, Da Mi.

453
00:26:57,050 --> 00:26:58,050
Mom is sorry.

454
00:27:18,540 --> 00:27:20,380
(Mission: Mompossible)

455
00:27:40,660 --> 00:27:42,770
This is something precious
to you, right?

456
00:27:42,770 --> 00:27:44,570
I received it from someone I love.

457
00:27:44,630 --> 00:27:45,840
He said he has a girlfriend.

458
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,440
They must be in
a long-term relationship.

459
00:27:48,070 --> 00:27:51,570
Ms. Kang Da Mi, I came to see you
because I have a favor to ask.

460
00:27:51,710 --> 00:27:52,810
This should be good enough, right?

461
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:55,080
But why am I so nervous?

462
00:27:55,350 --> 00:27:58,480
Mother,
I'm really worried about this.

463
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:00,320
Honey.

464
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:04,720
Dae Chi, someone is here to see you.
She is a very young and pretty lady.

465
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:06,220
Is that you, Su Yeong?

466
00:28:07,690 --> 00:28:09,660
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
